<title>PORTUGAL: Portugese business maintains uptrend in June.</title>
<headline>Portugese business maintains uptrend in June.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Retail and wholesale businesses reported further improvement in activity in June, continuing the upward trend begun in the second quarter of 1996, Portugal's National Statistics Institure (INE) said in its June survey.</p>
<p>&quot;In both sectors, business opinion on sales volume was more favourable than a year ago, and the same was true for projected suppliers' orders&quot;, it said.</p>
<p>Businessmen were also opimistic regarding commercial activity for the next few months, it added.</p>
<p>--Lisbon newsroom 3511-353-8254</p>
</text>
